    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d738">

                <pb facs="0817" n="697" xml:id="pg697"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.01 Foreign Control/168: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Greene</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-12T13:00:00-05:00">December 12, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>167. Your telegram No. 199, December 3, 3 p.m.<anchor n="55" xml:id="d738-f1"/>
                    Please transmit the following to the Secretary General: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The American member of the Committee appointed to study the problem
                            raised by the Liberian Government’s request for assistance has received
                            the note of the Secretary General, dated December 1, 1931,<anchor n="55"
                                xml:id="d738-f2"/> informing the members of the Committee that its
                            next meeting has been fixed for the middle of January.</p>
                        <p>In reply, the American Member has the honor to state that his Government
                            is prepared to participate in the session.”</p></quote></p>
                <p>You may add informally that Reber expects to sail on January 2 and to arrive in
                    Geneva about the 10th of the month.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
